{
  "name": "v8_decoder_matrix",
  "description": "fnet v8 component 3: instruction decode + 3x4 routing matrix, isolated (stims replace the port output buses). proc_decoder_matrix semantics: bits 1/2/4/8 route portA->out1..4, 16/32/64/128 portB->out1..4, 256/512/1024/2048 (instr>>12)->out1..4; probes are the matrix_out anchor constants. Plus explicit write-trigger checks: the sensor fires on bit 2 only (anything routed to write_value). The instruction rides $instr_stim; port data rides $mem[N] rows. Extended 2026-07-28 to cover the WHOLE crossbar and, more importantly, TWO SOURCES ON ONE OUT. The matrix is a full 3x4 crossbar and half its routes had never been driven; the six missing ones are here now, including a->out4, which is the conditional-relative-jump path. Summation is the keystone: values are NOT normalised inside the matrix (port A's value arrives on its own row signal, const's on the immediate carrier), so two sources sharing a signal sum on the wire while two carrying different signals both ride the net and are added later by the write path's each+0 relabel. That is what makes base+index addressing, add-immediate-in-flight and predicated writes possible without a single new instruction - the philosophy being programmable interconnect rather than opcodes.",
